Let first be "aabcc".
Let second be "dbbca".
Let third be "aadbbcbcac".
Let first size be the number of characters in first.
Let second size be the number of characters in second.
Let width be second size plus 1.
Let height be first size plus 1.
Let size be width times height.
Let table be a list of size zeros.
Set item 0 of table to 1.
For every row from 1 to first size.
If character (row minus 1) of first is character (row minus 1) of third and item ((row minus 1) times width) of table is 1, set item (row times width) of table to 1.

For every column from 1 to second size.
If character (column minus 1) of second is character (column minus 1) of third and item (column minus 1) of table is 1, set item column of table to 1.

For every row from 1 to first size.
For every column from 1 to second size.
Let index be row times width plus column.
Let spot be row plus column minus 1.
If character (row minus 1) of first is character spot of third and item (index minus width) of table is 1, set item index of table to 1.
If character (column minus 1) of second is character spot of third and item (index minus 1) of table is 1, set item index of table to 1.

Let last be one less than size.
If item last of table is 1, print true.
Otherwise, print false.
